# Loaded by `vite build` (mode=production), which is what Netlify runs.
#
# WHY THIS IS COMMITTED WHILE site/.env.local IS NOT
# This is the PBKDF2-SHA256 verifier, not the password. The site is static, so
# the check necessarily runs in the visitor's browser and this value is already
# inlined in the deployed JavaScript - anyone can read it with View Source. So
# keeping it out of git bought no secrecy at all, while guaranteeing the exact
# failure it caused: Netlify built without it, ADMIN_CONFIGURED came out false,
# and the logo silently stopped being an unlock entry point.
#
# What protects the password is the 210,000-iteration KDF, which makes each
# guess cost real work. See src/hooks/useAdmin.ts for the full threat model and
# what this does NOT protect (the JSON under /data stays fetchable either way -
# use `npm run build:team` when the separation has to be real).
#
# A real environment variable still wins: Vite gives existing env vars priority
# over .env files, so setting VITE_ADMIN_VERIFIER in Netlify overrides this
# without a commit. That is the way to rotate the password.
#
# Regenerate with: python scripts/set_admin_password.py
VITE_ADMIN_VERIFIER=210000:zCJfJeT/+AsyiLRvPpdrxg==:bTSRfDnhgAoQ9AkhwgGkXuA//pWAhliAiPmCR9esYS4=
